{
  "version": 3,
  "comment": "Canonical pixel-avatar definitions for the Raft agent avatar system (task #352). One file for every consumer: packages/web/src/components/agent/PixelAvatar.tsx and packages/server/src/services/pixelAvatarService.ts import it, and the web build serves it at /config/pixelAvatars.json for the mobile app. palette maps single letters to hex colors (_ = transparent). Each avatar grid is 8 rows of 8 palette letters; bg is a palette letter, or a literal #hex for one-off backgrounds (finch, mug, ottie). series groups the pickable avatars into themed sets of exactly 8, in picker order; every avatar not in reservedKeys is in exactly one series. avatars entries follow the series order, reserved keys last. reservedKeys are in no series and are excluded from AVATAR_KEYS (random pick + manual picker). The seeded-random avatar generator (mulberry32 identicons for pixel:random:seed) intentionally stays in code, not here. Bump version on every change: the mobile app ignores a downloaded document older than the one it bundles.",
